---
permalink: /svg/index.html
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{{ svg.title }}</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="SVG tracers ranked in one comparison: single colour and multicolour, with quality, complexity and documented sources."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://bench.voshart.com/svg/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/benchmark.css' | assetUrl }}" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/svg.css' | assetUrl }}" />
    <script>
      (function () {
        try {
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme =
            localStorage.getItem('bench-theme') ||
            (matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light');
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="svg-page">
    <main>
      <header class="hero">
        <div>
          <small class="eyebrow"
            ><a href="/">Voshart / Benchmarks</a> · <a href="/ocr/">OCR</a> ·
            <a href="/stt/">Speech</a></small
          >
          <h1>SVG tracer benchmarks</h1>
          <p>Quality, complexity and failures.</p>
        </div>
        <button
          class="quiet"
          id="themeToggle"
          type="button"
          aria-label="Toggle light and dark mode"
        >
          Theme
        </button>
      </header>
      <div class="controls svg-controls">
        <select id="svgMode" aria-label="Colour type">
          {% for mode in svg.matrix.modes %}
            <option
              value="{{ mode.id }}"
              {% if mode.id == svg.matrix.default_mode %}selected{% endif %}
            >
              {{ mode.label }}
            </option>
          {% endfor %}
        </select>
        <input
          id="svgSearch"
          type="search"
          placeholder="Search tracers…"
          aria-label="Search tracers"
        />
        <label class="svg-complexity"
          ><input id="svgComplexity" type="checkbox" /> Complexity</label
        >
        <button type="button" id="svgReset">Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="key" id="svgStatus" role="status">
        {{ svg.matrixResult.rows.length }} configurations · relative index
      </p>
      <div
        class="table-scroll"
        tabindex="0"
        role="region"
        aria-label="SVG tracer comparison; scroll horizontally for all datasets"
      >
        <table id="svgMatrix">
          <caption class="sr-only">
            One SVG tracer comparison. Relative index from matched tests. Exact configurations and
            sources in details.
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr id="svgHead">
              {{ svg.matrixResult | svgMatrixHead(svg) | safe }}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="svgRows">
            {{ svg.matrixResult | svgMatrixRows(svg) | safe }}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="key">
        ↑ higher · ↓ lower · — unavailable · ⓘ sources & details. Index is relative, not accuracy.
      </p>
      <p class="svg-difference-note">
        Our font scores differ from StarVector’s table.
        <button class="quiet" type="button" popovertarget="svg-differences">Compare ⓘ</button>
      </p>
      <div id="svg-differences" popover class="rank-note svg-detail">
        <button
          class="rank-note-close"
          type="button"
          popovertarget="svg-differences"
          popovertargetaction="hide"
          aria-label="Close score differences"
        >
          ×
        </button>
        <h3>Where our results differ</h3>
        {{ svg | svgDifferences | safe }}
        <p><a href="/svg/evidence/protocol-diagnostic.json">Diagnostic data</a></p>
      </div>
      <noscript
        ><p>
          All results and source details are shown. JavaScript enables filters, search, sorting and
          complexity columns.
        </p></noscript
      >
      <details class="method" id="methodology">
        <summary>Ranking, metrics & sources</summary>
        <p>
          The index uses the same finite-cohort percentile calculation as our speech benchmark. Each
          quality score is ranked only against configurations in its exact test, then averaged once
          per dataset family. The full font run takes priority over its overlapping pilot. Missing
          scores are not losses. Search and sorting do not change the index; changing colour type
          recalculates it from the selected datasets.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a qualified relative summary across different cohorts. Sparse coverage, publisher
          reports and unverified versions limit comparisons. Configurations remain separate rows; a
          paper baseline is not assumed equivalent to our installed version. The index does not
          establish a matched win between tracers tested on different protocols.
        </p>
        <p>
          Single colour includes fonts and binary PolyFit inputs. Multicolour includes colour and
          mixed datasets, including SVG-Icons; no flat-only or gradient-only result split is
          reported. The gradient filter stays unscored. This filters measurements, not claimed
          software capabilities.
        </p>
        <p>
          Complexity is optional and never affects the quality index. Segments, paths and tokens
          remain distinct units. Each complexity cell names its dataset in ⓘ; no cross-dataset mean
          is invented. Full precision determines the index; rounding is display-only.
        </p>
        <p>
          Local fonts use matched resvg renders: 256 px for DINOv2-base FP32, with all final-layer
          tokens averaged and cosine mapped to (cosine + 1) / 2; 1024 px for geometry, reported in
          native pixels. All images are retained. Empty output against a visible reference gets a
          256 px boundary penalty; blank against blank is zero. Conditional nonempty means are
          labeled separately. PolyFit inputs have no vector masters. Sampled topology is not exact
          vector certification.
        </p>
        <details class="comparison-note">
          <summary>Metric definitions</summary>
          <dl class="svg-definitions">
            {% for id, metric in svg.metrics %}
              <dt>{{ metric.label }}</dt>
              <dd>{{ metric.description }}</dd>
            {% endfor %}
          </dl>
        </details>
        <p>
          <a href="/svg/data.json" download="svg-tracer-results.json">Download data JSON</a> ·
          <a href="/svg/evidence/starvector-models-2025.csv">StarVector table CSV</a> ·
          <a href="/svg/evidence/published-tables-2025.json">Other published tables</a> ·
          <a href="/svg/evidence/full-fonts-summary.json">Full-run summary</a> ·
          <a href="/svg/evidence/provenance.json">Local provenance</a>
        </p>
        <details class="comparison-note">
          <summary>All sources</summary>
          <div class="source-grid">
            {% for id, source in svg.sources %}
              <p>
                <a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{{ source.title }}</a
                ><br /><small
                  >{{ source.operator }} · {{ source.attribution }}. {{ source.note }}</small
                >
              </p>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </details>
      </details>
      <p class="key svg-affiliation">{{ svg.affiliation }}</p>
      <footer>
        Evidence snapshot {{ svg.snapshot_date }} ·
        <a href="https://github.com/voshart/benchmarks/tree/main/data/svg"
          >Source data & methodology</a
        >
        · <a href="/">All benchmarks</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/pairwise-ranking.js' | assetUrl }}"></script>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/ranking.js' | assetUrl }}"></script>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/svg-comparison.js' | assetUrl }}"></script>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/svg-matrix.js' | assetUrl }}"></script>
    <script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/svg-page.js' | assetUrl }}"></script>
  </body>
</html>
